Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/openconfig/goyang v1.6.4-0.20251113201521-a80f2799d7b9

RFC 7950 Section 7.20.3.2: "If a property can only appear once, the property
MUST NOT exist in the target node." ApplyDeviate shared assignments for add
and replace, so add overwrote config, mandatory, units and list bounds.
The existing default guard is retained.

Keep explicit AST property presence separately from values, including false,
empty units, zero min-elements and unbounded max-elements. Check every
singleton before applying an add, then update presence after each applied
deviation so a second add cannot overwrite a property the first added.
Inherited config alone is not an explicit property. Section 14 permits no
type statement in deviate add, so type changes require deviate replace.

No upstream pull request is opened yet. Remove this patch when the pinned
upstream release includes the correction. Other goyang patches remain
separate; this diff changes neither the module dependency nor its source URL.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a vendored
module".

